Z||000000||Coop88||06-20-2001||05:51 AM||||For those of you who have replaced/changed your horns, what did you replace them with? I can't stand the sound of the horn on my formula, and my gf's dog runs up to her car when she honks the horn (the dog LOVES squeak toys). Basically, I'm looking for some recommendations. Thanks.||||reg||10
Z||000001||skitime||06-20-2001||06:08 AM||||I got my air horns from Harbor Freight and the volume is 135 db @ 1 meter and they only cost $18.00. I hate having stock horns that sound like every other GM car. A sports car should sound like a sports car. <A HREF="http://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=30980" TARGET=_blank>http://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=30980</A>  I have used them for years without a problem. The compressor is mounted at the same location as the stock horns (stock horns are still mounted but disconnected) The horns are bolted to the plastic inner wheel well with the end of the horns coming out just below the well. It is an easy simple install.  If you want to hear them go to this link and listen to them in the video. Its cool and you can really hear the difference between the V6s and the 4s as they go past. ftp://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/speedshot.zip<P><P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
